## llvm-driver's findTool matches argv[0] by suffix (see llvm-driver.cpp), so
## folding llvm-cov in as "cov" makes any name ending in "...cov" ambiguous
## against "sancov" (which also ends in "cov"). This only resolves correctly
## today because LLVMDriverTools.def happens to list "sancov" before "cov"
## (reverse-alphabetical order) -- verify both directions explicitly so a
## future reordering doesn't silently misroute one tool to the other.

## Don't make symlinks on Windows.
# UNSUPPORTED: system-windows
# REQUIRES: llvm-driver

# RUN: rm -rf %t
# RUN: mkdir %t
# RUN: ln -s %llvm %t/sancov
# RUN: ln -s %llvm %t/llvm-cov
# RUN: ln -s %llvm %t/cov

# RUN: %t/sancov --help | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SANCOV
# SANCOV: sancov [options] <action> <binary files...>

# RUN: %t/llvm-cov --help | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LLVM-COV
# RUN: %t/cov --help | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LLVM-COV
# LLVM-COV: Usage: llvm-cov {export|gcov|report|show} [OPTION]...
